# 0094-sheet-width-first-build-content-tab-pill-nas-listing.patch -- the owner's field report on dev.ibuilder.app (0093): points S, T, U, V. Applies after 0093.
# UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR: compiled, and its pure part ran in the host harness (below).
#
# S. The game sheet was WIDER than the screen (Delete, "Choose a cover…" and the segmented rows cut). Cause: the row "Update (build again with the update or DLC)" (shown while the build
#    lacks an update that is here: South Park after its first build, hence "it goes away once the update is added") had its title REQUIRED at its full width (compression 1000) while the
#    page's width to the screen is 999 (Theme.PinColumn): the title won and widened the whole page. Now a row's title wraps on 2 lines then truncates (SheetPriority.Title 900; the Sources
#    rows too), and the segmented rows are FitRows: label beside the control while both fit (SheetFit.Stacked), else the label above and the control on the whole width; each segment is as
#    wide as its own title (ApportionsSegmentWidthsByContent). Decided at every layout (any size class, the iPad's inspector).
# T. Updates and DLC came only with a SECOND build. Cause (the owner's log): the first build of South Park started while its update was still downloading (".nsz.part"), and the chain's
#    content signature even named the .part. Now every build (Library, Build tab, the queue: SetUpAndPlay) first WAITS for an update or DLC of the game still being copied in (it starts
#    when they have landed: StartBuildsAfterDownload), and FETCHES from the cloud the game's newer update and missing DLC (ContentFetch.ToFetch, any source) before it starts (one download,
#    then the build: "build: <game>: first its update v327680 from On the NAS (5.9 GB), then the build: it includes them"); the content signature never takes a .part. The Build row and the
#    card of a game not built say what its first build includes: "update v327680 · 1 DLC (On the NAS: 5.9 GB, fetched before the build)".
# U. The lit tab pill drew its gear over "Settings": its new configuration was laid out inside the animation of the page that was closing. The pills are now styled with no animation and laid
#    out at once (icon leading, label truncating); the same for the three tabs (the iPad's sidebar has no pill).
# V. The NAS listing now says what it holds: "NAS: 4 games, 2 updates, 3 DLC (1 classified by content)" (one line per listing, after the classification of 0091). A game on this iPhone whose
#    update or DLC is only in the cloud says so on its card ("update v327680 on the NAS") and its menu has "Download its update and DLC (5.9 GB)".
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-22, M1 Pro): check-patches-apply.sh: every patch 0010-0094 applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree. Compile
#   (-t:Compile): 0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code as before 0080. Host harness (harness94: … P93;P94): 358 of 358 checks (16 new: the rows' widths at 320/375/393 pt with
#   the longest strings, the priorities, the tab pills, the .part, the fetch, the Build line, the listing line, the menu entry, the wiring); 12 of 12 mutations killed.
# NOT VERIFIED: nothing ran on a device: the sheet's real layout (the widths are estimated, not measured with UIKit), the tab pill after a pushed page, a real first build with its update.
# NEW UI STRINGS: "Download its update and DLC (", ", fetched before the build)", " on the NAS"; log lines " classified by content)", "build: … waits for ", ": first its ",
#   "its update and DLC are here, the build starts".
